lassification condition."},{"excerpt":"must have been available for work (with an exception for temporary illness)","claim":"A person must have been available for work, except in cases of temporary illness.","category":"scope","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"was available for work except for temporary illness","narrative":"must have been available for work, except for temporary illness","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The availability condition and temporary-illness exception match the source.","materiality":"A core classification condition."},{"excerpt":"and must have actively looked for work during the four weeks ending with that week.","claim":"A person generally must have actively searched for work during the four-week period ending with the reference week.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"made an active job search effort in the four-week period ending with that week","narrative":"Active search must fall within the four-week period ending with the reference week","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The search activity and four-week period match the source; the next sentence states the layoff exception.","materiality":"A core classification condition and time window."},{"excerpt":"There’s an exception to the job-search requirement: someone on temporary layoff who expects to be recalled may qualify without actively searching.","claim":"A person on temporary layoff who expects recall may be classified as unemployed without actively searching.","category":"scope","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"or was temporarily laid off and expected recall","narrative":"A temporarily laid-off person expecting recall","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source explicitly allows expected recall from temporary layoff as an alternative to active job search.","materiality":"Material exception to the active-search requirement."},{"excerpt":"But browsing job listings alone doesn’t count as actively looking.","claim":"Browsing job listings, without other search activity, does not count as active job search.","category":"interpretation","label":"U insufficient evidence to settle","evidence":"Passive-only job search does not count as active search.","narrative":"someone whose only job-search activity was browsing listings. The first may qualify without an active search; passive browsing alone does not meet the active-search requirement.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source says passive-only search is not active, but does not specify whether browsing listings alone is classified as passive-only.","materiality":"Material to the article’s contrast between qualifying and nonqualifying search activity."},{"excerpt":"Availability, what happened during the reference week, and job-search activity during the four-week period all affect whether someone is counted as unemployed","claim":"Availability, employment status during the reference week, and job-search activity during the four-week period affect whether a person is counted as unemployed.","category":"scope","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"an unemployed person was not employed during the survey reference week, was available for work except for temporary illness, and made an active job search effort in the four-week period ending with that week or was temporarily laid off and expected recall.","narrative":"availability and the survey reference periods also matter","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The sentence summarizes the source’s classification conditions and periods.","materiality":"Summarizes the conditions that determine classification."},{"excerpt":"and included in the rate’s denominator.","claim":"Being counted as unemployed means being included among the unemployed people in the unemployment-rate denominator.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The unemployment rate divides unemployed people by the sum of employed and unemployed people.","narrative":"whether a person is counted among the unemployed in the rate’s denominator","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"propagated","explanation":"The source denominator includes the unemployed population.","materiality":"Connects classification to the rate calculation."}]}

